  "family": "vernacular",
  "lineage": "Unaccompanied cattle-driving vocal genre of the Brazilian sertão — Ceará, Pernambuco, Bahia and Piauí — sung by vaqueiros to move and calm herds, documented from the colonial period and recorded ethnographically from the mid-20th century: free-meter melismatic aboio on open vowels and long descending glissandi, mixolydian and neutral-third inflections, and rhymed toada verses about drought, cattle and the leather-clad rider, sometimes answered by the herd's bells.",
